course: dictionary
lesson: 13283
title: A short word with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Grad is a short, informal word. The full word is graduate, which means a person who has finished high school, college or university. Informal words are common in talk and on social media, but you may not find them in every book.
explain: Many short words have more than one meaning. «My cousin is a new grad, so the family is having a party for her.» Here the words party and finished show that grad means a person who has finished their studies. Always read the words around a word to find the right meaning.
explain: Grad can also be a part of longer words, such as «grade» and «gradual». Notice that «grad» is the start of those words, but they do not always mean the same thing. When you are not sure, check the sentence and the dictionary.
fact: «Grad» is a short, informal word for graduate.
fact: «Grad school» means a school for study after university.
fact: In the USA and Canada, «grad» can also mean the graduation party or ceremony.
fact: A grad is also a small unit for measuring angles: 100 grads make a right angle, but degrees are used much more.
fact: Informal words are fine in chat with friends, but use the full word, such as graduate, in school writing.
exercise: «My cousin is a new grad, so the family is going to a party for her.» What does grad mean here? | A kind of small cake | A word for a teacher | A measure of how hot something is | *A person who has finished school or college
exercise: Ella asks, «Is grad school for little children?» What is grad school? | *A school for study after university | A school with no lessons at all | A school for babies | A school for dancing only
exercise: Angles can be measured in grads. How many grads make a right angle? | 10 | 4 | 360 | *100
test: Which word is a short, informal way of saying graduate? | *grad | gradual | gravel | grade
test: «The grad party was full of balloons and music.» What is a grad party most likely? | A party for a dog's birthday | A maths lesson | *A party to celebrate finishing school | A football match
exam: «She is going to grad school after she finishes university.» Where is she going next? | *To a school for study after university | To a shop to buy bread | Back to nursery | To her first day at primary school
